        },
        "5": {
          "id": "5",
          "name": "documentation.md",
          "language": "md",
          "contents": "Disney Character API\n====================\n\n\n_id\n  The unique identifier for the character.\n  Type: integer\n\nurl\n  The API endpoint URL for the character.\n  Type: string\n\nname\n  The name of the character.\n  Type: string\n\nsourceUrl\n  The link to the character's source/fandom page.\n  Type: string\n\nfilms\n  A list of films the character has appeared in.\n  Type: list [string]\n\nshortFilms\n  A list of short films the character has appeared in.\n  Type: list [string]\n\ntvShows\n  A list of TV shows the character has appeared in.\n  Type: list [string]\n\nvideoGames\n  A list of video games the character has appeared in.\n  Type: list [string]\n\nalignment\n  The character's affiliation (e.g., hero or villain).\n  Type: string\n\nparkAttractions\n  Disney park attractions featuring the character.\n  Type: list [string]\n\nallies\n  A list of the character's known allies.\n  Type: list [string]\n\nenemies\n  A list of the character's known enemies.\n  Type: list [string]",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "5",
        "4",
        "3"
      ]
    },
    "bubble_choice_description": "Explore the Disney characters database API and create your own custom dashboard.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/0283296f6a7f6700f0a7056a714fe895-Screenshot 2026-01-28 at 1.08.22 PM.png",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore The Disney Characters Database\r\n\r\n1. Skim the official Disney Characters documentation in `documentation.md`.\r\n   \r\n2. Then look at the JSON response for a single character in `disney.json` to figure out how the data is structured. \r\n\r\n3. Use AI Tutor to help you modify your code to display different information (like \"allies\" or \"TV shows\").\r\n\r\n\r\n**Hint**: You can upload files like `disney.json` to use when prompting AI Tutor.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n:::details [Not sure how to modify the code?]\r\n\r\nTry one of the following prompts:\r\n\r\n- In the file `disney.json`, how do I access the \"vote\\_average\" to show the rating?\r\n- How do I change the code to display the \"release\\_date\" in a more readable format?\r\n- What is the difference between \"popularity\" and \"vote\\_count\"? \r\n:::",
